l activity volume or node popularity \u2014 indeed these nodes are low-degree (2-5 events each). The same node set had no triangles at all in the preceding window, ruling out a static/pre-existing structure, and wedge edges are single-occurrence rather than repeated traffic. Explicit ordering for node 111 (111->504 @45369, 504->821 @45721, closing 111->821 @45860) confirms the closing interaction follows its support. Caveat: the wave is thin (13 triangles, one per node) and spread over the window rather than concentrated in one burst, hence confidence below 0.9."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion:** The signature is present and specific.\n\nKey findings:\n- **Target nodes:** 13 triangles, **12 closed within 800** (fraction 0.923), median closing lag **474** \u2014 every one of the 12 listed nodes contributes a promptly-closed wedge (step_03, step_04).\n- **Confounder \u2014 global base rate:** graph-wide in the same window only 38.3% of 253 triangles close within 800, median lag 1348 (step_06). So promptness is not a property of the window itself.\n- **Confounder \u2014 popularity/volume:** the target nodes are *not* hubs (2\u20135 events, 2\u20135 distinct partners each; step_05), while the actual top-activity hubs (28, 1583, 524, \u2026) close only 26.6% within 800 with median lag 1677 (step_07). High volume produces *worse* promptness, so the effect is not volume-driven.\n- **Confounder \u2014 static connectivity / pre-existing pattern:** in the preceding equal-length window the same nodes have **zero** triangles (step_08), so this is not a standing structural artifact.\n- **Mechanism check:** node 6's wedge edges (6\u2013843, 843\u2013879) each occur exactly once (step_09, step_10), i.e. genuine single-shot wedges, not repeat traffic. For 111 the wedge-then-close ordering is explicit: 111\u2192504 @45369, 504\u2192821 @45721, then the closing 111\u2192821 @45860 (step_11) \u2014 a 139-unit lag.\n- Tightening delta to 200 keeps 3 closures (step_12), and activity is flat (1\u20137 events/bin, no single burst; step_13), so the closures are distributed prompt events rather than one coincidental spike.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_afa3f67f\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"closure_wave\",\n  \"entities\": [6, 10, 17, 37, 57, 72, 80, 87, 106, 111, 114, 116],\n  \"window\": [43373, 55373],\n  \"confidence\": 0.83,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Within [43373,55373] the 12 named nodes each anchor a wedge whose third edge arrives promptly: 12/13 triangles close within 800 units, median lag 474. This is far above the window's own base rate (38%, median 1348) and above the rate for the window's most active hubs (27%, median 1677), so it cannot be explained by overall activity volume or node popularity \u2014 indeed these nodes are low-degree (2-5 events each). The same node set had no triangles at all in the preceding window, ruling out a static/pre-existing structure, and wedge edges are single-occurrence rather than repeated traffic. Explicit ordering for node 111 (111->504 @45369, 504->821 @45721, closing 111->821 @45860) confirms the closing interaction follows its support. Caveat: the wave is thin (13 triangles, one per node) and spread over the window rather than concentrated in one burst, hence confidence below 0.9.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 41063, "total_output_tokens": 3981, "total_tokens": 45044, "total_latency_ms": 58826, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}